## Prefill and TTFT

| | model (mfu 0.5) | measured | ratio |
|---|---|---|---|
{% for r in P.prefill.model_vs_measured %}
{% if r.mfu == 0.5 %}
| 1M-token prefill, {{ r.config }} | {{ r.model_s|n(2) }} s | {{ r.measured_s }} s | {{ (r.measured_s/r.model_s)|n(1) }}x |
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}

The reported prefill runs {{ P.prefill.fit_k_tp4|n(1) }}x slower than our roofline model. Scaling the model
by that factor on TP4 mispredicts TP8 by {{ "%+.0f"|format(P.prefill.pred_tp8_err_pct) }}%: measured TP4→TP8 speedup is
{{ P.prefill.measured_tp_speedup|n(2) }}x; the model says {{ P.prefill.model_tp_speedup|n(2) }}x. So the prefill path has large costs we do not
model, and **prefill is not a calibrated result**. MDA-1 is decode-only by design. TTFT keeps prefill
on the GPU pool and adds the KV hand-off (400 Gb/s RDMA assumed):

| scenario | GPU TTFT | hybrid TTFT (GPU prefill → MDA-1) | KV handed off |
|---|---|---|---|
{% for r in P.ttft.scenarios %}
| {{ r.scenario }} | {{ (r.gpu_ttft_s*1000)|n(0) }} ms | {{ (r.hybrid_ttft_s*1000)|n(0) }} ms | {{ r.kv_mb|n(1) }} MB ({{ r.kv_handoff_ms|n(2) }} ms) |
{% endfor %}

TTFT is unchanged, as intended. For the short prompt the scaled model gives {{ (P.ttft.scenarios[0].gpu_ttft_s*1000)|n(0) }} ms
against the README's client-side 40 ms (which also includes HTTP and tokenization). The prefill
scaling factor, fitted at 1M tokens, over-predicts short prompts.
TTFT figures are therefore indicative only.
